      "status": "CORRECT",
      "conclusion": "The actual native criterion computes bidirectional box-to-token/token-to-box terms with its existing token maps, background masks and temperature, then divides by num_boxes. The total ScanRefer loss weights each of seven heads by 0.5/7. The captured matcher result at index 1 is the last head because the native order is proposal_, last_, 0head_ through 4head_. The added correction is 0.5/7*(native(expanded,N+A)-native(original,N)); adding it once to the native loss replaces the old last term. N+A rescales original, new and background contributions together, exactly as the plan says.",
